Six p orbitals at the three 3c sites of a simple cubic cell, a pair at each
site perpendicular to the site's own axis: the orbitals at the three sites
are one another's images.

1. the model: a p pair at each 3c site, perpendicular to the site's own axis
   site              axis   orbitals
   (0, 0.5, 0.5)     x      py, pz
   (0.5, 0, 0.5)     y      px, pz
   (0.5, 0.5, 0)     z      px, py
   bands            : 6, from 6 orbitals
   hoppings         : 66, random, to every orbital within one lattice constant,
                      averaged over the operations of T_d

2. the group: what the point set allows, and what the hoppings obey
   point set allows : #221.93 Pm-3m1'
   realized group   : #215.71 P-43m1', orbitals at Wyckoff 3c
   broken           : i, 3 like m(z), 6 like C2([110]), 6 like C4(z), 8 like S3([111]),
                      each also with time reversal: 48 of the 96 coset representatives
                      of the lattice translations
   each site's axis : C4(x), C4(y), C4(z) broken; S4(x), S4(y), S4(z) kept
   the operations broken are inversion times those kept: each site loses the fourfold
   rotation about its own axis and keeps the -4 rotoinversion about it

3. r.rep.characters: the atomic-limit table, what each orbital carries
   orbital  Wyckoff  site symmetry  function  irrep     named by  determined by  orbital characters
         0       3c           -42m                E  point group    hamiltonian  E=+2, C2(y)=0, C2(x)=-2, m([011])=0, S4(x)=0
         1       3c           -42m                E  point group    hamiltonian  E=+2, C2(y)=0, C2(x)=-2, m([011])=0, S4(x)=0
         2       3c           -42m                E  point group    hamiltonian  E=+2, C2(x)=0, C2(y)=-2, m([101])=0, S4(y)=0
         3       3c           -42m                E  point group    hamiltonian  E=+2, C2(x)=0, C2(y)=-2, m([101])=0, S4(y)=0
         4       3c           -42m                E  point group    hamiltonian  E=+2, C2(z)=-2, C2(x)=0, m([110])=0, S4(z)=0
         5       3c           -42m                E  point group    hamiltonian  E=+2, C2(z)=-2, C2(x)=0, m([110])=0, S4(z)=0
     orbitals 0-5 at 3c induce the elementary band representations of T1 at 1b (-43m) + T2 at 1b (-43m)   (.band_representations)
   C3([111])        : carries each site onto the next, and its axis onto the next site's
   (0, 0.5, 0.5)    : onto (0.5, 0, 0.5), axis x onto y, C2(x) onto C2(y), character -2 at both
   (0.5, 0, 0.5)    : onto (0.5, 0.5, 0), axis y onto z, C2(y) onto C2(z), character -2 at both
   (0.5, 0.5, 0)    : onto (0, 0.5, 0.5), axis z onto x, C2(z) onto C2(x), character -2 at both
   each site's characters are the first site's, carried by the operations of the orbit,
   and each row is the E of its own site's -42m

4. the same model, every pair rotated inside itself by 0.37 rad
   realized group   : #215.71 P-43m1'
   rep.characters   : section 3's atomic-limit table, line for line
   all 6 bands      : GM4 + GM5 + M1 + M2 + 2×M5 + R4 + R5 + X1 + X2 + 2×X5
   all 6, rotated   : GM4 + GM5 + M1 + M2 + 2×M5 + R4 + R5 + X1 + X2 + 2×X5
   the rotation is a change of orbital basis inside each pair, a choice of Wannier gauge,
   and a character is a trace, which no change of basis moves

5. the six bands as a sum of elementary band representations
   atomic limit     : 1 x T1↑G(3)@1b(-43m1',-43m) + 1 x T2↑G(3)@1b(-43m1',-43m)
   both bases       : largest energy difference 0.000000 along GM-X-M-GM-R-X, the figure's path
   E at 3c of P-43m1' is one of the known exceptions to an irrep at a maximal
   Wyckoff position inducing an elementary band representation

